6 Overall rules
═══════════════

  1. The beginning/default portion of a file continues the most previous
     section, whether it was in a parent or child inclusion.
  2. Nested includes are relative to the nesting level, but sequenced
     includes are relative to the current file (although see rule 1).
  3. minlevel is absolute for the file it includes, although the section
     nesting will return to the place it was when the include ends
     (although subsequent sections in the including file will be nested
     under the included file).
  4. Metadata like `#+TITLE' and `#+AUTHOR' are concatenated (this is
     the same as if there were multiple metadata elements in the same
     file: i.e. inclusion has no effect).
  5. Relative paths specified in `#+INCLUDE:' directives are relative to
     the file they are contained in.
